\begin{align*}
V_s &= \frac{4}{3}\pi r^3 \\
&= \frac{4}{3}\pi (\frac{s}{2})^3 \\
&= \frac{4}{3}\pi \frac{s^3}{8} \\
&= \frac{\pi s^3}{6}
\end{align*}

The volume $V_c$ of the cube with side length $s$ is given by the formula $V_c = s^3$. Therefore, the ratio of the volume of the inscribed sphere to the volume of the cube is:

\begin{align*}
\frac{V_s}{V_c} &= \frac{\frac{\pi s^3}{6}}{s^3} \\
&= \boxed{\frac{\pi}{6}}
\end{align*}
